  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "The complex number $z$ satisfying the equation $|z-i|=|z+1|=1$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "vZCgh",
      "text": "0",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "URVMm",
      "text": "$1+i$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "giAdB",
      "text": "$-1+i$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "zkrPa",
      "text": "$1-i$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have, $|z-i|=|z+1|=1$\r\nLet, $\\quad z=x+iy$\r\n$\\therefore \\quad|z-i|=1$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad|x+iy-i \\mid=1$\r\n$\\Rightarrow|x+(y-1) i|=1$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad x^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=1$\r\nAlso, $\\quad|z+1|=1$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad|x+ iy+1 \\mid=1$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad|(x+1)+i y|=1$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad(x+1)^{2}+y^{2}=1$\r\nFrom Eqs. (i) and (ii), we get $x=y=0$ and $x=-1, y=1$\r\n$\\therefore \\quad z=0,-1+i$",
    "image": null
  },
